One of the Norse kennings for Tyr was the Thingtyr,
the Thing God.

The Icelandic thing evolved into parliment.  The Saxon
thing evolved into trial by jury.  Many nations now
use these two descendents of the same tradition.  In
the US there are annual county fairs that are also
descended from the same tradition.  That tradition is
probably common in much of Europe as well - a regional
gathering with displays/contests of agriculture and
handicrafts plus contests and carnival.

